KZ3 patch 2198 (RSX pass 171, S7.4 of the S7 design, host tests only, nothing calls it): the resident-stream core.
Pure, API-neutral code for resident raw vertex streams (the GPU reads the guest's raw vertex bytes in place from a pool of
4 KB blocks, one current block per guest page and write generation), with no D3D12 / Vulkan / Win32 calls, no walker
types, no switch, and no wiring into the live renderer (S7.5 backends and S7.6 wiring come later).
  libs/kzr/core/vres/kzr_vres.h        page pool, block lists, walker epochs, acquire hold, fence-safe allocation (spare
    FIFO + clock), page copies as jobs (copy_seq / done_seq, need_seq for the draw's reads gate), the write generation
    behind kzr_wgen_ops {collect, arm, clean}, the draw table writer.
  libs/kzr/core/vres/kzr_vres_decode.h the decode through the block lists, text in the C/HLSL common subset.
  libs/video/rsx_vtx_res.h             bridge to patch 2076's rsx_vg_draw plan and the HLSL head/tail text (text only).
Origin: design input from Killzone 2 (patches 6079 rsx_vtx_res.h and 6080, the Killzone 2 port's runtime work): the model, the
block rules, the epoch stand and the two pass 91b rules (stamp again at record, acquire hold). Rewritten for kzr; credit
in NOTICE at the public export.
Host test: tools/smoke/test_vres.sh (decode equal to 2076's over 3,000 draws, 300,000-step residency stress with delayed
page copies, directed cases, eleven negative controls incl. a stale-reuse shape found in the Killzone 2 port).

